# QVAC documentation is required

Before using, changing, or advising on any QVAC feature, read the matching section in the local docs copy:

`.cursor/docs/llms-full.txt`

Source: https://docs.qvac.tether.io/llms-full.txt

This includes `@qvac/sdk`, Bare runtime wiring, plugins (e.g. llama.cpp completion), model constants and load/unload, `complete` / generation params, embeddings, RAG, multimodal, and any other QVAC API or config.

## How to check

1. Search the local file for the feature, API, model constant, plugin, or config you need.
2. Read that section. Do not rely on memory or another project's QVAC usage.
3. Follow the documented API, imports, and Bare/Node requirements. If this repo already diverges, prefer the docs unless a comment explains a deliberate exception.
4. Do not load the entire file — it is large. Search, then read the relevant headings.

## Examples

```js
// ❌ BAD — invent or recall an SDK call from memory
import { qvac } from '@qvac/sdk'
await qvac.chat(prompt)

// ✅ GOOD — search llms-full.txt for the feature (e.g. "Running on Bare",
// "loadModel", the plugin name) and copy the documented imports and calls.
```
